    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-δοσία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προδίδωμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>abandonment in need, betrayal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1633
			</span></i>: mostly in Prose, <i>treason,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προδοσίην συντίθεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.88
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				8.128
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκευάζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.100
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προδοσίας ἁλούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					24.127
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				443a
			</span></i>(pl.).</div>
